WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.459
Time Warner Audiobooks presents

00:00:06.459 --> 00:00:08.900
Rich Dad, Poor Dad

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:13.160
Written by Robert Kiyosaki with Sharon L. Lecter, CPA

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:15.339
And read by Stephen Hoy

00:00:15.339 --> 00:00:18.519
Featuring an introduction by Robert Kiyosaki

00:00:18.519 --> 00:00:26.800
I had two fathers, a rich one and a poor one.

00:00:27.399 --> 00:00:29.160
One was highly educated and intelligent.

00:00:29.739 --> 00:00:34.159
He had a Ph.D. and completed four years of undergraduate work in less than two years.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:36.640
The other father never finished the eighth grade.

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:41.119
Both men were successful in their careers, working hard all their lives.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:43.780
Both earned substantial incomes.

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:46.079
Yet one struggled financially all his life.

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:52.039
The other would become one of the richest men in Hawaii. One died leaving tens of millions

00:00:52.039 --> 00:00:58.740
of dollars to his family, charities, and his church. The other left bills to be paid. Both men

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:05.959
were strong, charismatic, and influential. Both men offered me advice, but they did not advise the same things.

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:11.659
Both men believed strongly in education, but did not recommend the same course of study.

00:01:12.519 --> 00:01:17.519
If I had had only one dad, I would have had to accept or reject his advice.

00:01:18.459 --> 00:01:26.319
Having two dads advising me offered me the choice of contrasting points of view, one of a rich man and one of a poor man.

00:01:27.159 --> 00:01:32.819
Instead of simply accepting or rejecting one or the other, I found myself thinking more,

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:39.519
comparing, and then choosing for myself. The problem was, the rich man was not rich yet,

00:01:39.959 --> 00:01:45.159
and the poor man not yet poor. Both were just starting out on their careers,

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:48.260
and both were struggling with money and families.

00:01:51.859 --> 00:01:52.680
But they had very different points of view about the subject of money.

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:55.260
For example, one dad would say,

00:01:57.739 --> 00:01:58.400
the love of money is the root of all evil.

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:03.219
The other, the lack of money is the root of all evil.

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:09.659
As a young boy, having two strong fathers, both influencing me, was difficult.

00:02:14.919 --> 00:02:15.740
I wanted to be a good son and listen, but the two fathers did not say the same things.

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:20.000
The contrast in their points of view, particularly where money was concerned,

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:23.580
was so extreme that I grew curious and intrigued.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:28.780
I began to start thinking for long periods of time about what each was saying.

00:02:30.979 --> 00:02:31.560
Much of my private time was spent reflecting,

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:33.659
asking myself questions such as,

00:02:34.699 --> 00:02:35.259
Why does he say that?

00:02:38.099 --> 00:02:38.900
and then asking the same question of the other dad's statement.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:41.740
It would have been much easier to simply say,

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:44.060
Yeah, he's right. I agree with that.

00:02:46.039 --> 00:02:52.560
Or to simply reject the point of view by saying, the old man doesn't know what he's talking about. Instead, having two dads whom I

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:58.219
love force me to think and ultimately choose a way of thinking for myself. As a process,

00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:02.259
choosing to think for myself turned out to be much more valuable in the long run,

00:03:02.939 --> 00:03:06.699
rather than simply accepting or rejecting a single point of view.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:11.120
One of the reasons the rich get richer, the poor get poorer,

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:13.300
and the middle class struggles in debt

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:17.639
is because the subject of money is taught at home, not in school.

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:20.740
Most of us learn about money from our parents.

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:24.099
So what can a poor parent tell their child about money?

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:25.319
They simply say,

00:03:25.639 --> 00:03:31.460
stay in school and study hard. The child may graduate with excellent grades, but with a poor

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:37.159
person's financial programming and mindset. It was learned while the child was young.

00:03:38.319 --> 00:03:42.759
Money is not taught in schools. Schools focus on scholastic and professional skills,

00:03:42.979 --> 00:03:45.280
but not financial skills. This explains how smart bankers, doctorsastic and professional skills, but not financial skills.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:49.419
This explains how smart bankers, doctors, and accountants,

00:03:53.639 --> 00:03:54.280
who are in excellent grades in school, may still struggle financially all their lives.

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:03.080
Our staggering national debt is due in large part to highly educated politicians and government officials making financial decisions

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:05.000
with little or no training on the

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:10.340
subject of money. I often look ahead to the new millennium and wonder what will happen when we

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:15.340
have millions of people who will need financial and medical assistance. They will be dependent

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:20.060
upon their families or the government for financial support. What will happen when Medicare

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:26.339
and Social Security run out of money? How will a nation survive if teaching children about money

00:04:26.339 --> 00:04:33.379
continues to be left to parents, most of whom will be, or already are, poor? Because I had two

00:04:33.379 --> 00:04:39.180
influential fathers, I learned from both of them. I had to think about each dad's advice, and in

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:45.259
doing so, I gained valuable insight into the power and effect of one's thoughts on one's life.

00:04:46.019 --> 00:04:48.740
For example, one dad had a habit of saying,

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:50.259
I can't afford it.

00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:53.180
The other dad forbade those words to be used.

00:04:53.819 --> 00:04:56.860
He insisted I say, how can I afford it?

00:04:57.220 --> 00:04:59.800
One is a statement and the other is a question.

00:05:00.519 --> 00:05:03.319
One lets you off the hook and the other forces you to think.

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:07.660
My seem-to-be-rich dad would explain that by automatically saying the words,

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:10.759
I can't afford it, your brain stops working.

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:15.720
By asking the question, how can I afford it, your brain is put to work.

00:05:16.399 --> 00:05:18.480
He did not mean buy everything you wanted.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:23.860
He was fanatical about exercising your mind, the most powerful computer in the world.

00:05:24.459 --> 00:05:27.680
My brain gets stronger every day because I exercise it.

00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:30.699
The stronger it gets, the more money I can make.

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:33.579
He believed that automatically saying,

00:05:33.899 --> 00:05:36.879
I can't afford it, was a sign of mental laziness.

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:39.699
Although both dads worked hard,

00:05:40.279 --> 00:05:43.699
I noticed that one dad had a habit of putting his brain to sleep

00:05:43.699 --> 00:05:45.180
when it came to money matters, and the other had a habit of putting his brain to sleep when it came to money matters,

00:05:45.699 --> 00:05:48.139
and the other had a habit of exercising his brain.

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:53.639
The long-term result was that one dad grew stronger financially and the other grew weaker.

00:05:53.959 --> 00:05:59.060
It is not much different from a person who goes to the gym to exercise on a regular basis

00:05:59.060 --> 00:06:02.779
versus someone who sits on the couch watching television.

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:05.600
Proper physical exercise increases

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:10.920
your chances for health, and proper mental exercise increases your chances for wealth.

00:06:11.879 --> 00:06:18.399
Laziness decreases both health and wealth. My two dads had opposing attitudes and thought.

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:30.360
One dad thought that the rich should pay more in taxes and take care of those less fortunate. The other said, taxes punish those who produce and reward those who don't produce.

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:35.540
One dad recommended, study hard so you can find a good company to work for.

00:06:36.079 --> 00:06:40.180
The other recommended, study hard so you can find a good company to buy.

00:06:41.180 --> 00:06:45.240
One dad said, the reason I'm not rich is because I have you kids.

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:46.980
The other said,

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:50.079
The reason I must be rich is because I have you kids.

00:06:50.959 --> 00:06:55.220
One dad encouraged talking about money and business at the dinner table.

00:06:55.800 --> 00:06:59.660
The other forbade the subject of money to be discussed over a meal.

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:01.319
One said,

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:04.959
When it comes to money, play it safe and don't take risks.

00:07:05.560 --> 00:07:07.740
The other said, Learn to manage risk. One said, when it comes to money, play it safe and don't take risks. The other said, learn to manage risk.

00:07:08.519 --> 00:07:12.560
One believed, our home is our largest investment and our greatest asset.

00:07:13.379 --> 00:07:15.620
The other believed, my house is a liability,

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:19.120
and if your house is your largest investment, you're in trouble.

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:21.879
Both dads paid their bills on time,

00:07:22.399 --> 00:07:25.939
yet one paid his bills first while the other paid his bills last.

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:34.060
Being a product of two strong dads allowed me the luxury of observing the effects different thoughts have on one's life.

00:07:34.779 --> 00:07:38.680
I noticed that people really do shape their life through their thoughts.

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:46.120
For example, my poor dad always said, I'll never be rich. And that prophecy became reality.

00:07:46.839 --> 00:07:53.019
My rich dad, on the other hand, always referred to himself as rich. He would say things like,

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:59.319
I'm a rich man, and rich people don't do this. Even when he was flat broke, after a major

00:07:59.319 --> 00:08:05.740
financial setback, he continued to refer to himself as a rich man. He would cover himself by saying,

00:08:06.439 --> 00:08:13.019
there is a difference between being poor and being broke. Broke is temporary and poor is eternal.

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:21.379
My poor dad would also say, I'm not interested in money or money doesn't matter. My rich dad

00:08:21.379 --> 00:08:27.420
always said, money is power. The power of our thoughts may never be measured or appreciated,

00:08:27.939 --> 00:08:32.919
but it became obvious to me as a young boy to be aware of my thoughts and how I expressed myself.

00:08:33.399 --> 00:08:37.379
I noticed that my poor dad was poor not because of the amount of money he earned,

00:08:37.759 --> 00:08:41.320
which was significant, but because of his thoughts and his actions.

00:08:41.720 --> 00:08:44.159
As a young boy, having two fathers,

00:08:44.539 --> 00:08:45.919
I became acutely aware of

00:08:45.919 --> 00:08:52.639
being careful which thoughts I chose to adopt as my own. Whom should I listen to? My rich dad

00:08:52.639 --> 00:08:59.820
or my poor dad? Although both men had tremendous respect for education and learning, they disagreed

00:08:59.820 --> 00:09:05.480
in what they thought was important to learn. One wanted me to study hard, earn a degree, and get a good

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:11.240
job to work for money. He wanted me to study to become a professional, an attorney, or an

00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:16.639
accountant, or to go to business school for my MBA. The other encouraged me to study to be rich,

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:22.740
to understand how money works, and learn how to have it work for me. I don't work for money,

00:09:23.019 --> 00:09:25.960
were the words he would repeat over and over. Money works

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:33.200
for me. At the age of nine, I decided to listen to and learn from my rich dad about money. In doing

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:39.080
so, I chose not to listen to my poor dad, even though he was the one with all the college degrees.

00:09:39.940 --> 00:09:47.740
Once I made up my mind whom to listen to, my education about money began. My rich dad taught me over a period of 30 years, until I was age 39.

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:51.639
He stopped once he realized that I knew and fully understood

00:09:51.639 --> 00:09:55.019
what he had been trying to drum into my often thick skull.

00:09:55.879 --> 00:10:00.659
Money is one form of power, but what is more powerful is financial education.

00:10:01.320 --> 00:10:02.960
Money comes and goes.

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:05.860
But if you have the education about how money works,

00:10:06.100 --> 00:10:12.340
you gain power over it and can begin building wealth. The reason positive thinking alone does

00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:18.740
not work is because most people went to school and never learned how money works, so they spend

00:10:18.740 --> 00:10:24.299
their lives working for money. Because I was only nine years old when I started, the lessons my rich

00:10:24.299 --> 00:10:25.399
dad taught me were simple.

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:27.320
And when it was all said and done,

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:30.960
there were only six main lessons repeated over 30 years.

00:10:31.460 --> 00:10:33.720
This book is about those six lessons.

00:10:34.259 --> 00:10:38.720
Put as simply as possible as my rich dad put forth those lessons to me.

00:10:39.379 --> 00:10:42.580
The lessons are not meant to be answers, but guideposts.

00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:45.120
Guideposts that will assist you and your

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:50.620
children to grow wealthier, no matter what happens in a world of increasing change and uncertainty.

